sommelier: give every bind of an output the same position

sommelier makes one sl_host_output per client bind of wl_output and lays
them out left to right, each at the sum of the widths before it. A client
that binds an output twice, like Firefox (once through GTK, once in its
own Wayland code), sees one monitor at x=0 and a second copy to its
right. With that layout, Firefox ignores its saved window size and opens
at 500x200 every time.

Entries for the same host output share its position, and the list is
sorted by it. Give them the same virt_x, and only advance past an output
once.

diff --git a/vm_tools/sommelier/sommelier-output.cc b/vm_tools/sommelier/sommelier-output.cc
index 8512765..4ef14c7 100644
--- a/vm_tools/sommelier/sommelier-output.cc
+++ b/vm_tools/sommelier/sommelier-output.cc
@@ -283,14 +283,24 @@ void sl_output_get_dimensions_original(struct sl_host_output* host,
 void sl_output_update_output_x(struct sl_context* ctx) {
   // Outputs are positioned in a line from left to right based off their x
   // position.
+  // There's one sl_host_output per client bind, so a client that binds the
+  // same output twice has two entries for it. They share the host's
+  // position (the list is sorted by x): give them the same virt_x, or the
+  // second copy looks like another monitor to the right of the first.
   int next_output_x = 0;
+  struct sl_host_output* prev = nullptr;
   for (auto output : ctx->host_outputs) {
+    bool same_output = prev && prev->x == output->x && prev->y == output->y;
+    int virt_x = same_output ? prev->virt_x : next_output_x;
     // Update the value and mark for sending.
-    if (output->virt_x != next_output_x) {
-      output->virt_x = next_output_x;
+    if (output->virt_x != virt_x) {
+      output->virt_x = virt_x;
       output->needs_update = true;
     }
-    next_output_x += output->virt_rotated_width;
+    if (!same_output) {
+      next_output_x += output->virt_rotated_width;
+      prev = output;
+    }
   }
 }
 
